# ---- Data provider selection ----
# ALL OF THESE ARE OPTIONAL. With no env vars at all the app loads the real league
# (NSL Fantasy Hoops) with player photos on, so a Vercel deploy needs zero config.
#
# sleeper (DEFAULT) | fixture (offline synthetic demo) | csv
# LEAGUE_PROVIDER=fixture

# ---- Database (OPTIONAL) ----
# Used ONLY to persist decision-ledger annotations. All read features work without
# it, and leaving this UNSET is a first-class setup: the ledger keeps your note for
# the session and says plainly that it was not persisted.
#
# prisma/schema.prisma is on `provider = "postgresql"`, so this must be a
# postgres:// URL - local, Neon, Supabase, whatever. A `file:./dev.db` value used to
# sit here uncommented and does NOT work against that provider: since D36 a
# DATABASE_URL that is set but unusable answers a write with 500 and "Your note was
# NOT saved", which is the honest answer and not one you want to clone into.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/parquet?schema=public"

# ---- Multi-user seats (OPTIONAL) ----
# UNSET = SINGLE-USER MODE, and that is the default. With no AUTH_SECRET the app
# behaves exactly as it always has: whoever opens it can capture reasoning as
# whichever team they are currently viewing. Correct for one person running Parquet
# for themselves, wrong the moment the link is shared with the league.
#
# Set it to any long random string (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`) to require a SIGNED
# SEAT for private authorship. The "viewing as" lens is unaffected - every public
# number stays readable as any team, by anyone, which is the point of the lens.
#
# Onboarding, once it is set:
#   1. pnpm claim-links https://your-deployment   # prints one link per manager
#   2. open your own link to claim your seat
#   3. /commissioner then shows the same list in-app, for handing out the rest
# Rotating this value invalidates every seat at once. That is also how you revoke one.
# AUTH_SECRET=
#
# `pnpm claim-links` takes the deployment origin as a CLI arg (above); PARQUET_ORIGIN
# is only a fallback default for that script when the arg is omitted, and is never
# read by the app itself.
# PARQUET_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# ---- Sleeper (only used when LEAGUE_PROVIDER=sleeper) ----
# Committed as defaults in lib/providers/index.ts - only set these to override.
# SLEEPER_USERNAME=EZ8
# SLEEPER_LEAGUE_ID=1347007735815766016

# ---- CSV (only used when LEAGUE_PROVIDER=csv) ----
# Directory of the documented CSV export (lib/providers/csv/). Required - the CSV
# provider throws at startup without it.
# CSV_DIR=./data/csv

# ---- Analyst LLM (OPTIONAL, free / open-source) ----
# Point at ANY OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint:
#   • Groq (free hosted open models):  https://api.groq.com/openai/v1  + LLM_API_KEY
#   • OpenRouter (free tier):          https://openrouter.ai/api/v1     + LLM_API_KEY
#   • Local Ollama (fully offline):    http://localhost:11434/v1        (no key)
# With nothing set, the Analyst runs a deterministic, still-adversarial audit.
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# ---- LLM tracing (OPTIONAL, OFF by default, and read the warning) ----
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY turns on lib/observability/trace.ts, which posts every analyst
# LLM call to LangSmith. LANGSMITH_PROJECT names the project the runs land in; with
# it unset they go to "default". Unset key = clean no-op, no request, no cost.
#
# WHAT ENABLING IT SENDS. A traced run carries the FULL analyst prompt, and that
# prompt includes the viewer's OWN captured reasoning from the decision ledger -
# the one genuinely private thing in this app. Every other number Parquet shows is
# league data the whole league can already read; those notes are not. Turning this
# on hands them to a third party. Opt-in on purpose, and it should stay off unless
# you own the LangSmith account and accept exactly that.
# LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
# LANGSMITH_PROJECT=parquet

# ---- Player photos ----
# Sleeper's headshots are not licensed for redistribution - personal/local use only.
# This is a HOTLINK (an <img src> pointed at Sleeper's own CDN), never a copy this
# app stores or serves itself, which is what keeps that personal-use posture honest.
# Default is OFF, and stays OFF for a fork you haven't reviewed this note in - a
# public repo with no env vars at all must render monograms, not someone else's
# unlicensed headshots. Set to "true" (exactly that string; anything else is OFF) to
# opt in for your own deploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_PLAYER_PHOTOS=false

# ---- NBA team logos ----
# NOT gated by a flag, unlike the headshots above - a team crest (components/TeamLogo.tsx)
# is a hotlinked trademark, not a person's likeness, and `TeamAvatar`'s manager avatars are
# already unflagged for the same reason (D49). Always on, no config needed.

# ---- Debug timings (OPTIONAL) ----
# Set to "1" to log cold-load duration for the two heaviest loaders (corpus assembly
# in lib/history.ts, the draft index in lib/lineage/index.ts) as `[timing] <label>:
# <ms>ms`. Costs nothing when unset. This is the measurement that tells you when
# cold-start latency has grown enough to justify a persistent cache (the next stage),
# rather than guessing.
# PARQUET_DEBUG_TIMINGS=1
